      "writtenOn": "2022-02-22T06:10:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "run-app commands accepts \"APP config\" which is by intention to deliver `os: \"microdroid\"` (which is the only supported type for now). Virtualization service uses this to determine the pre-configured OS images.\n\n- app config: for a VM app which is supposed to be run on microdroid (at least for now).\n- raw config: for a VM app which uses any bootloader OR kernel/initrd.\n\nWe could extend \"app config\" to be overridable like..\n\n```\n{\n  \"os\": \"microdroid\",            // VS uses ./etc/microdroid.json\n  \"bootloader\": \"my_bootloader\", // overrides \"bootloader\" in ./etc/microdroid.json\n  ..\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ad797040_d8a2ba83",
